### ============================================
### WEBSERV: STATIC FILE HANDLER TEST SUITE
### ============================================
### Description: In-depth tests for serving static files and directories.
### Assumes a server running on port 8090 with a file structure like:
###   /var/www/html/
###     - index.html
###     - style.css
###     - script.js
###     - cutecat.png
###     - no_read_permissions.txt (chmod 000)
###     /subdir/
###       - page.html
###     /autoindex_on/
###       - file1.txt
###       - file2.txt
###     /autoindex_off_no_index/
###       - secret.txt
### ============================================

### Variables
@host = localhost
@port = 8090
@baseUrl = http://{{host}}:{{port}}
@userAgent = WebServ-Test-Client/1.0

### ============================================
### Section 1: Basic File Retrieval (200 OK)
### ============================================

### Test 1.1: Get root index file
# Expects: 200 OK with content of index.html
GET {{baseUrl}}/index.html
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 1.2: Get a CSS file
# Expects: 200 OK with Content-Type: text/css
GET {{baseUrl}}/style.css
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 1.3: Get a JavaScript file
# Expects: 200 OK with Content-Type: application/javascript
GET {{baseUrl}}/script.js
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 1.4: Get a PNG image
# Expects: 200 OK with Content-Type: image/png
GET {{baseUrl}}/cutecat.png
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 1.5: Get a file from a subdirectory
# Expects: 200 OK with content of page.html
GET {{baseUrl}}/subdir/page.html
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 1.6: Get a gif from a subdirectory
# Expects: 200 OK with content of op.gif
GET {{baseUrl}}/blogs/op.gif
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### ============================================
### Section 2: Directory Handling
### ============================================

### Test 2.1: Request directory root with implicit index
# A GET on "/" should serve the index file from the root location.
# Expects: 200 OK with content of index.html
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 2.2: Request subdirectory without trailing slash
# Should trigger a 301 redirect to add the trailing slash.
# Expects: 301 Moved Permanently, Location: /subdir/
GET {{baseUrl}}/subdir
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 2.3: Request subdirectory with trailing slash
# Should serve the index file from that subdirectory.
# Expects: 200 OK with content of subdir/index.html (if it exists)
GET {{baseUrl}}/subdir/
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 2.4: Directory with autoindex ON
# Location is configured with "autoindex on" and has no index file.
# Expects: 200 OK with an HTML body listing directory contents.
GET {{baseUrl}}/autoindex_on/
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 2.5: Directory with autoindex OFF and no index file
# Location is configured with "autoindex off" and has no index file.
# Expects: 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/autoindex_off_no_index/
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### ============================================
### Section 3: Error Handling (4xx Status Codes)
### ============================================

### Test 3.1: File Not Found
# Requesting a file that does not exist.
# Expects: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/non_existent_file.html
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 3.2: Directory Not Found
# Requesting a directory that does not exist.
# Expects: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/non_existent_directory/
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 3.3: File with No Read Permissions
# Requesting a file that exists but server lacks read permissions for.
# Expects: 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/no_read_permissions.txt
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 3.4: Path Traversal Attempt
# Attempting to access a file outside of the configured root directory.
# Expects: 400 Bad Request or 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/../../../../etc/passwd
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 3.5: Method Not Allowed
# Using POST on a resource handled by StaticFileHandler.
# Expects: 405 Method Not Allowed with an "Allow: GET" header.
POST {{baseUrl}}/index.html
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 4

test

### Test 3.6: Method Not Allowed (DELETE)
# Using DELETE on a resource handled by StaticFileHandler.
# Expects: 405 Method Not Allowed with an "Allow: GET" header.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/index.html
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### ============================================
### Section 4: Redirects
### ============================================

### Test 4.1: Location-level Redirect
# Assumes a location block like: location /old-page.html { redirect 301 /new-page.html; }
# Expects: 301 Moved Permanently, Location: /new-page.html
GET {{baseUrl}}/old-page.html
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 4.2: Directory Trailing Slash Redirect with Query String
# The redirect should preserve the query string.
# Expects: 301 Moved Permanently, Location: /subdir/?param=value
GET {{baseUrl}}/subdir?param=value
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### ============================================
### Section 5: Edge Cases
### ============================================

### Test 5.1: Request with URL-encoded characters
# Server should correctly decode the path.
# Expects: 200 OK with content of style.css
GET {{baseUrl}}/%73%74%79%6c%65%2e%63%73%73
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 5.2: Request for a file with a space in the name
# Assumes a file named "my file.txt" exists.
# Expects: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/my%20file.txt
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Test 5.3: Request for a hidden file (dotfile)
# Depending on server rules, this might be allowed or forbidden.
# Expects: 200 OK or 403 Forbidden/404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/.hiddenfile
Host: example.com
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
```// filepath: tests/static_handler_tests.http
